function loadMemoSample(){let t=`NORTHSTAR SPECIALTY PACKAGING — FICTIONAL SAMPLE DEAL SOURCE
Company: Northstar Specialty Packaging. Fictional U.S. specialty packaging platform seeking $12 million of growth equity. This is invented training material only.
Business overview: Manufactures rigid and short-run custom packaging for food, personal care and healthcare customers. Operations are in the U.S. Midwest and Southeast. Management reports 60% repeat-order revenue and 78% capacity utilization; these statements are unverified.
Financial performance: FY2023 revenue $21.5M and EBITDA $2.7M. FY2024 revenue $24.6M and EBITDA $3.4M. FY2025 revenue $28.0M and EBITDA $4.2M. FY2025 EBITDA margin 15.0%. All figures are fictional, unaudited and unverified. No audited statements or quality-of-earnings report provided.
Market opportunity: Management cites demand for recyclable rigid packaging and short-run custom formats. No third-party market study, TAM/SAM/SOM analysis, regional forecast, trade-flow data or source-backed market growth estimate has been provided.
Global landscape and value chain: Suppliers, resin/input-cost exposure, manufacturing capacity, logistics, regional competition and end-market demand require independent research. No global peer map or supply-chain study provided.
Customers and competition: Customer concentration, customer retention, churn, gross margins by customer/product, market share, competitors, pricing benchmarks, win/loss data and customer interviews have not been provided.
Growth plan: Seeking $12M for a new production line, working capital and a potential regional add-on acquisition over 12–18 months. Capex quotes, forecast, ramp assumptions, add-on target details and quantified value-creation plan not provided.
Management team: Management biographies, operating track record, references, incentives, ownership, board structure and succession plan not provided.
Transaction: Minority growth equity preferred. Valuation, ownership offered, governance terms, liquidation preferences, control rights, investor return targets and detailed use-of-proceeds allocation not provided.
Risks and mitigation: Potential diligence areas include input-cost pass-through, customer concentration, capacity ramp, environmental and safety compliance, working-capital seasonality, integration risk and market demand. No risk-control plan has been independently validated.
Valuation and returns: No valuation method, public peer set, transaction comps, IRR/MOIC model, dilution analysis, exit multiple or return waterfall provided.
Exit strategy: Potential strategic or sponsor sale routes are only hypotheses; no buyer universe, timeline or exit analysis provided.
Diligence priorities: Obtain audited financials and monthly accounts; quality-of-earnings review; customer concentration/retention and margins; capex budget; compliance review; working-capital schedule; management references; market study; peer and transaction comps; valuation and ownership proposal; exit and returns analysis.
IMPORTANT: All company names, figures and transaction details are fictional and for software testing only. Do not distribute as an actual deal.`;document.getElementById('memoText').value=t;document.getElementById('memoFileStatus').textContent='Loaded fictional Northstar sample with memo sections and explicit diligence gaps';activeFileName='Fictional Northstar sample source';toast('Sample source loaded. Generate a memo to see the full investment committee structure.');}
